{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_metricsextension", "label": "MetricsExtension", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": "Die Metrics-Extension", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bis enable() gerufen wird ist die Registry eine Noop-Implementierung, damit eine App ohne Monitoring keinen Overhead traegt. Nur DevTools schaltet sie temporaer ein und ruft beim Detach disable() - eine selbst eingeschaltete Registry wird nie hinter dem Ruecken abgeschaltet."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_counter", "label": "Counter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": "Counter", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Monoton - negative Inkremente werfen. Fuer Werte die sinken koennen ist ein Gauge das richtige Primitiv, nicht ein Counter."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_gauge", "label": "Gauge", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": "Gauges", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_histogram", "label": "Histogram", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": "Histogramme", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Es gibt kein eigenes Timer-Primitiv - eine Operation wird gemessen, indem ihre Dauer in ein Histogram beobachtet wird. Buckets sollen das SLO abbilden; die Defaults sind Sekundenskala."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_labels", "label": "Labels", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": "Labels", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Labels machen aus einer Metrik viele Zeitreihen - jede eindeutige Label-Kombination ist zur Export-Zeit eine separate Serie."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_cardinality_discipline", "label": "Kardinalitaetsdisziplin", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": "Kardinalitaetsdisziplin", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unbeschraenkte Labels (Request-ID, User-ID, Zeitstempel) produzieren unbeschraenkte Serien und lassen dem Monitoring-System den Speicher ausgehen. Ziel: unter 100 Serien pro Metrik."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_bucketize", "label": "bucketize", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": "bucketize - den Wert an der Quelle beschraenken", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bildet einen von aussen kommenden Label-Wert auf eine feste Allow-List ab, sonst auf 'other' - die Familie kann also nie mehr als allowed.length + 1 Serien halten, egal was ein Angreifer schickt. Das ist die eigentliche Loesung; die Registry-Grenze ist nur das Auffangnetz."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_maxseriesperfamily", "label": "maxSeriesPerFamily (Kardinalitaetsgrenze)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": "Die Kardinalitaetsgrenze", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Auffangnetz fuer Labels die niemand beschraenkt hat: ab der Grenze (Default 10000) faltet die Familie alles weitere in eine Overflow-Serie und loggt einmal pro Familie. Der Marker steckt im Label-WERT, nicht im Label-Namen, weil Prometheus Label-Namen mit __-Praefix beim Ingest entfernt und die Overflow-Serie sonst still in eine echte Serie mischen wuerde. Default 10000 statt ~1000, weil actor_mailbox_size{path} und ein Per-pid-Projektions-Fan-out genau waehrend einer Stoerung am breitesten sind - dem Moment, in dem man sie lesen muss. 0 schaltet ab (nicht Infinity: die Grenze ist eine Ganzzahl)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_metricsregistryoptions", "label": "MetricsRegistryOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": "Die Kardinalitaetsgrenze", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_metricsextension", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_counter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_metricsextension", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_gauge", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_metricsextension", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_histogram", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_metricsextension", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_labels", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_labels", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_cardinality_discipline", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_bucketize", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_cardinality_discipline", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_bucketize", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_maxseriesperfamily", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_maxseriesperfamily", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_metricsregistryoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_maxseriesperfamily", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_stock_metrics_actor_mailbox_size", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_metrics_core_metrics_maxseriesperfamily", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_security_cluster_security_registry_caps", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}